content.text:
I found two places the family can walk into. Brooklyn Children's Museum is left out because its page doesn't say which ages it suits. Both sets of hours come from the venues' own sites. The ticket and date notes below are things the family should know before going.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), Upper West Side",
      "age_fit": "children ages 0-6",
      "when": "Tuesday-Sunday, 10 am-5 pm",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Central Park Zoo (includes the Tisch Children's Zoo)",
      "age_fit": "Child (3 - 12) ticket; Child (2 & under) free",
      "when": "Mon-Fri 10:00am-5:00pm, weekends 10:00am-5:30pm (April 2 - Oct 31, 2026 hours); last entry 1 hour before closing",
      "price": "$16.95 child (3-12), $22.95 adult for Zoo Admission; 2 and under free",
      "source_name": "Central Park Zoo"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **CMOM:**

I found three places a family can walk into on September 12 to 15 with a preschooler. I read each one's hours off its own site.

I'm assuming the dates are Sat Sept 12 to Tue Sept 15, 2026. If the trip is a different year, check the days against each site.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), 212 West 83rd Street",
      "age_fit": "children ages 0-6",
      "when": "Tuesday-Sunday, 10 am-5 pm; daily programs include Circle Time at 10:30 am",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Central Park Zoo (includes the Tisch Children's Zoo)",
      "age_fit": "Not stated as an age band on the zoo's own page",
      "when": "Opens 10 am daily; closes 5 pm Mon-Fri and 5:30 pm on weekends; last entry 1 hour before closing",
      "source_name": "Central Park Zoo"
    },
    {
      "name": "New York Aquarium, 602 Surf Avenue, Coney Island",
      "age_fit": "Child (3 - 12) ticket; Child (2 & Under) free",
      "when": "Daily Sept 8 to Oct 31: opens 10 am, last entry 4 pm, closes 5 pm",
      "price": "Child (3-12) $25.95 off-peak, $27.95 peak",
      "source_name": "New York Aquarium"
    }
  ]
}
```

I found two places the family can turn up to on those dates. Sept 12 is a Saturday and Sept 15 is a Tuesday.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), 212 West 83rd Street",
      "age_fit": "children ages 0-6",
      "when": "Open Tuesday-Sunday 10am-5pm, so Sat Sept 12, Sun Sept 13 and Tue Sept 15; closed Mon Sept 14",
      "price": "$18 at the door, $17 online (adults and children 1-18)",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Central Park Zoo (with the Tisch Children's Zoo)",
      "age_fit": "Child (3-12) ticket; children 2 and under free",
      "when": "Open daily 10am; closes 5:30pm on weekends (Sept 12-13) and 5pm on weekdays (Sept 14-15); last entry 1 hour before closing",
      "price": "Zoo Admission $16.95 for a child 3-12 ($9.95 Limited Admission, online only)",
      "source_name": "Central Park Zoo (Wildlife Conservation Society)"
    }
  ]
}
