I searched this and found three places a preschooler can walk into. I only had a few searches, so I did not get to playgrounds or the New York Aquarium.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), The Tisch Building, 212 West 83rd Street",
      "age_fit": "children ages 0-6",
      "when": "July-September: Monday-Sunday, 10 am-5 pm, so open Sept 12-15 on their schedule",
      "price": "Tickets $1 cheaper online; amount not on the pages I read",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Central Park Zoo (includes the Tisch Children's Zoo)",
      "age_fit": "Child (3 - 12) ticket; Child (2 & under) free",
      "when": "Their 2026 season (Apr 2-Oct 31) runs Mon-Fri 10:00-5:00, weekends 10:00-5:30; Sept 2027 hours not posted yet",
