- **CMOM:**

I found two venues a family with a preschooler can turn up to, each read off its own site. Neither site posted hours for the exact dates of September 12 to 15, so the hours below are their regular hours.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), The Tisch Building, 212 West 83rd Street",
      "age_fit": "ages 0-6",
      "when": "Regular hours 10 am-5 pm, Tuesday-Sunday. Its FAQ lists Monday-Sunday 10 am-5 pm for July-September, but the current pages say Tuesday-Sunday. The Sept 12-15 dates themselves are not confirmed.",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Preschool Place at New York Hall of Science (NYSCI), 47-01 111th St, Queens",
      "age_fit": "For children 6 and under, with their grownups",
      "when": "General hours Wednesday-Sunday 10 am-5 pm. Preschool Place's last entry is 4:30 pm and it closes at 4:45 pm. The page does not list Monday or Tuesday, so a visit on those days is unlikely to work. The Sept 12-15 dates are not confirmed.",
      "source_name": "New York Hall of Science"
    }
  ]
}
```

